A||||3||CW85T-Type||Did I really mess up? (Rear wheel bearing)||||1||
Z||000000||CW85T-Type||10-02-2000||04:18 PM||||Ok, I was finishing putting my izusu 5spd in this weekend.  Well, I forgot to put the Pas side axle in when putting the tranny back on (GRRRR).  Ok, so I seperate the ball joint, go to remove the lower contorl arm and it won't go.  SOooo I decide to get a better angle I wll remove the dust shield for the brakes (3 bolts).  Now when I put it back togehter it SEEMS to go together fine but as soon as I hand tighten the bolts for the dust shield the axle wont turn.<P>What did I do?<P>I checked the bearing/hub assembly is near $60 :P<P>Ouch..<P>Thanks,<BR>Chris Wilson<BR>1985 Buick Regal T-Type<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero SE||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||10-03-2000||12:05 AM||||I'm not sure I understand what's happening.<P>Will the axel turn if the dust shield bolts are not hand tightened?  Is the dust shield bent and rubbing against the hub or rotor when the bolts are tightened?||||reg||1
Z||000002||CW85T-Type||10-03-2000||12:22 AM||||The hub will not turn when I hand tighten the bolts (the dust shield bolts are the same ones that hold the hub/bearing in.<P>I read somewhere (after) that the bolts MUST go back in the same hole they came out of or you must replace the bearing (which is a whole bearing/hub assembly)<P>Chris||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||10-03-2000||02:39 AM||||We have removed and then reinstalled original rear bearing hubs and did not have any problems. I don't think the same bolts to same holes is correct. The only thing I can think of is if you did not remove the center hub bolt, that the bearing hub is not seating straight. There is an O ring that is on the hub and you may have damaged it. I would try loosening the bolts, then put the bolts in but turn each bolt 1/2 turn each at a time. This should make sure the hub is being installed evenly. Also you could try it without the brake dust shield to see if it is seating correctly. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||1
